{
 "Under the fast-track procedure, the tribunal shall consist of a sole arbitrator, the dispute shall be decided on written pleadings, documents, and submissions unless the tribunal considers an oral hearing necessary, and the award shall be made within six months of the tribunal entering upon the reference.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Fees for fast-track arbitration are payable as provided in the Schedule of Fees.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Making of Arbitral Award and Decision-Making": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "In a tribunal of more than one arbitrator, any decision shall be made by a majority. Questions of procedure may be decided by the presiding arbitrator if so authorised by the parties or the other arbitrators.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "As soon as possible after the last hearing or the last authorised submission, the tribunal shall declare the proceedings closed as to the matters to be decided in the award and inform the Secretariat and the parties of the date by which it expects to submit its draft award. No further submission or evidence may be made after closure unless the tribunal requests or authorises it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The award shall be made within twelve months from the date on which the tribunal enters upon the reference, which the parties may by consent extend by up to six months, in accordance with Section {0}A of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Form, Contents, and Dating of Award": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The award shall be in writing and signed by the members of the tribunal, or by a majority with the reason for any omitted signature stated. It shall state the reasons on which it is based, unless the parties have agreed otherwise or the award is on agreed terms.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The award shall state its date and the seat of arbitration, and shall determine interest and costs in accordance with Sections {0}({1}) and {2}A of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Before signing, the tribunal shall submit the draft award to the Secretariat, which may draw attention to matters of form without affecting the tribunal's liberty of decision. A signed copy shall be delivered to each party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Termination of Arbitral Proceedings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The proceedings terminate with the final award, or by order of the tribunal where the claimant withdraws its claim (unless the respondent objects and the tribunal recognises a legitimate interest in a final settlement), where the parties agree to terminate them, or where the tribunal finds that their continuation has become unnecessary or impossible.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where the parties fail to pay the deposits required under the Schedule of Fees, the tribunal may suspend or terminate the proceedings in respect of the claim or counter-claim concerned.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Correction, Interpretation, and Additional Awards": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Within thirty days of receiving the award, a party may, with notice to the other party, request the tribunal to correct any computational, clerical, or typographical error, or, if the parties so agree, to give an interpretation of a specific point or part of the award.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A party may, within the same period, request an additional award as to claims presented in the proceedings but omitted from the award.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The tribunal shall make the correction or give the interpretation within thirty days, and any additional award within sixty days, of receiving the request.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter VII</1>Mediation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Commencement of Mediation Proceedings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Mediation commences when a party's request for mediation is accepted by the other party, or on the date fixed by the parties' agreement to mediate.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where the other party does not accept the request within fifteen days, the requesting party may treat the request as rejected.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Selection, Appointment, and Independence of Mediator": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The parties may agree on a mediator from the Panel. Failing agreement within fifteen days, the Secretariat shall appoint a mediator having regard to the subject matter of the dispute.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Before accepting the appointment, the mediator shall sign a statement of acceptance, availability, impartiality, and independence, and disclose in writing any circumstance that may give rise to doubts as to their independence or impartiality. A party may object to an appointment made by the Secretariat within fifteen days of being notified of it, in which case the Secretariat shall appoint another mediator.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Conduct of Mediation Sessions and Private Caucuses": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The mediator may meet the parties jointly or separately, and may communicate with each party in private session.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Information given to the mediator in a private session shall not be disclosed to the other party without the consent of the party that gave it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Role of Mediator and Facilitation Protocol": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The mediator shall assist the parties in an independent and impartial manner to reach an amicable settlement of their dispute, treating them with fairness. The mediator shall not impose a settlement.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "After consulting the parties, the mediator shall promptly issue a written note setting out the manner in which the mediation will be conducted. Each party shall act in good faith throughout the mediation.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The mediator may, at the request of the parties, make suggestions as to options for settlement.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Mediated Settlement Agreement (MSA) and Finality": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where the parties reach a settlement, it shall be reduced to writing and signed by the parties and authenticated by the mediator.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where the parties so agree, the settlement may be executed as a settlement agreement under Section {0} of the Act, so as to have the status and effect of an arbitral award on agreed terms under Section {1} of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Mediation terminates on the signing of a settlement agreement; on a party's written notice that it withdraws; on the mediator's written notice that, in the mediator's opinion, further efforts are unlikely to resolve the dispute; or on the expiry of the agreed period for the mediation. The Secretariat shall confirm the termination to the parties in writing.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Without-Prejudice Privilege and Confidentiality": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Every statement, proposal, admission, and document made or exchanged in mediation is made without prejudice and is confidential. The fact that a mediation is taking place is not confidential.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Unless the law requires otherwise, no party shall rely in any other proceeding on any view or suggestion made by another party regarding settlement, any admission made in the mediation, any proposal made by the mediator, or the fact that a party indicated its willingness to accept a proposal.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The mediator shall not act as an arbitrator, representative, or counsel of a party in any proceeding relating to the dispute, and shall not be presented as a witness, save as the law otherwise provides.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter VIII</1>Conciliation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Commencement of Conciliation and Notice": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A party initiating conciliation shall send the other party a written invitation to conciliate, briefly identifying the subject of the dispute.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Conciliation commences when the other party accepts the invitation in writing. If the other party rejects the invitation, or does not reply within thirty days, there shall be no conciliation proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Appointment and Role of Conciliators": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "There shall be one conciliator unless the parties agree that there shall be two or three. The parties may agree on the conciliator from the Panel, failing which the Secretariat shall appoint the conciliator.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The conciliator shall assist the parties in an independent and impartial manner, guided by principles of objectivity, fairness, and justice, giving consideration to the rights and obligations of the parties and the circumstances surrounding the dispute.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Conciliator's Proposals for Settlement": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The conciliator may, at any stage of the proceedings, make proposals for a settlement of the dispute. Such proposals need not be in writing and need not be accompanied by reasons.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where it appears to the conciliator that there exist elements of a settlement acceptable to the parties, the conciliator shall formulate the terms of a possible settlement and submit them to the parties for their observations.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Settlement Agreement and Enforceability": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where the parties reach agreement, they shall draw up and sign a written settlement agreement, which the conciliator shall authenticate and furnish to each party.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The settlement agreement shall be final and binding on the parties and shall have the same status and effect as an arbitral award on agreed terms, in accordance with Sections {0} and {1} of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Termination of Conciliation Proceedings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Conciliation terminates on the signing of the settlement agreement; by a written declaration of the conciliator, after consulting the parties, that further efforts are no longer justified; or by a written declaration of a party that the proceedings are terminated.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The conciliator shall not act as an arbitrator, representative, or counsel of a party in any arbitral or judicial proceeding in respect of the dispute, and views, proposals, and admissions made in conciliation shall not be relied on in any such proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter IX</1>Specialized Corporate ADR": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Shareholder, Board, and Intra-Corporate Disputes": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Disputes between shareholders, between shareholders and the company, between directors, or among promoters, arising under a shareholders' agreement, articles of association, or joint venture agreement, may be referred under this Code to the extent that they are capable of settlement by arbitration or other ADR under the applicable law.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Secretariat shall, where practicable, appoint neutrals with experience in corporate governance, and may propose mediation as a first step where the parties' continuing relationship is at stake.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Cross-Border and Multi-Jurisdictional Commercial ADR": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "In an international commercial dispute, the parties may agree on the seat, the language, and the law applicable to the substance of the dispute and to the arbitration agreement. Failing agreement on the law applicable to the substance, the tribunal shall apply the rules of law it considers appropriate.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "A sole or presiding arbitrator in an international commercial arbitration shall, where any party so requests, be of a nationality other than that of the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "High-Value Financial and M&A Dispute Resolution": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "In disputes arising from financial transactions, mergers, acquisitions, and investments, including disputes over price adjustments, earn-outs, and warranty claims, the tribunal may, after consulting the parties, appoint an independent expert to determine specified accounting or valuation questions.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The tribunal may make such orders as are appropriate for the protection of commercially sensitive information, including confidentiality rings.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Intellectual Property and Technology Dispute Protocol": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "In disputes concerning intellectual property, technology, licensing, and information systems, the Secretariat shall, where practicable, appoint neutrals with technical expertise relevant to the dispute.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The tribunal may order inspection of source code, systems, or products under protocols that protect trade secrets, and its award shall bind only the parties and shall not affect the validity of any intellectual property right as against third parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter X</1>Implementation and Enforcement": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Implementation and Enforcement of Awards and Settlements": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The parties undertake to carry out every award and settlement without delay.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "An award shall be enforced in accordance with Section {0} of the Act, in the same manner as if it were a decree of a court.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Recognition and Enforcement Outside India": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "On the request of a party, the Secretariat shall furnish certified copies of the award and the arbitration agreement, and such certificates as to the conduct of the proceeding as may be required for recognition and enforcement of the award in another country under the New York Convention.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter XI</1>Costs & Fees": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Fees of the Institute and of Neutrals": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The filing fee, administrative fee, and the fees of arbitrators and other neutrals shall be as set out in the Schedule of Fees in force on the date of commencement of the proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The tribunal and administrative fees shall be fixed on the basis of the claim or counter-claim, whichever is higher. For disputes that cannot be quantified, the Secretariat shall fix the fee having regard to the facts of the case.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "No neutral shall accept any fee or payment from a party other than through, or as directed by, the Secretariat.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Deposits and Allocation of Costs": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The parties shall deposit the fees in the instalments set out in the Schedule of Fees, in equal shares unless the Schedule provides otherwise. Where a party fails to pay its share, the other party may pay it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The costs of the arbitration comprise the fees of the Institute and of the tribunal, the fees and expenses of any expert appointed by the tribunal, and the reasonable legal and other costs incurred by the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The tribunal shall, in its award, determine the costs of the arbitration and which party shall bear them, in accordance with Section {0}A of the Act, having regard to the conduct of the parties, including the extent to which each has conducted the arbitration in an expeditious and cost-effective manner, the outcome, and any offer of settlement.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Where all claims are withdrawn or the proceeding ends before a final award, the Secretariat shall fix the fees payable to the Institute and the neutral, and any refund due.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "<1>Chapter XII</1>Miscellaneous": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Confidentiality and Publication": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Institute, the neutral, and the parties shall keep confidential all matters relating to the proceeding, except the award where its disclosure is necessary for its implementation, enforcement, or a challenge to it, or as required by law.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Institute may publish anonymised extracts of awards for educational purposes, unless a party objects within thirty days of the award.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Code of Ethics, Disqualification, and Grievance Redressal": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Every neutral shall comply with the Preamble of this Code. A neutral who breaches it may be removed from the Panel, in addition to any other consequence under this Code or the law.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Any party, neutral, or member who believes that this Code has been breached may file a written grievance with the Secretariat, which shall be considered and decided by a committee of the Institute independent of the proceeding concerned. The decision shall be communicated to the complainant in writing.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Exclusion of Liability": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "No neutral, and neither the Institute nor any of its officers or staff, shall be liable to any person for any act or omission in connection with a proceeding under this Code, save for conscious and deliberate wrongdoing.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Amendments, Repeal, and Savings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Institute may amend this Code from time to time. An amendment shall apply to proceedings commenced after it comes into force, unless the parties agree otherwise.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Practice Directions": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Secretariat may issue practice directions, consistent with this Code, on matters of procedure and administration. Practice directions shall be published before they take effect.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "In all matters not expressly provided for in this Code, the Institute, the neutrals, and the parties shall act in the spirit of this Code and shall make every effort to ensure that every award and settlement is enforceable at law.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "— End of The Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, {0} —": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Download the {0} PDF": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Read the {0} edition": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Contents of the {0} Code": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "Link to Section {0}": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2018",
 "The Adjudix Rule Book · Second Edition": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Builds on {0} by bringing every proceeding online through the Adjudix E-Portal.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Builds on the {0} edition — {1} new sections, each marked <1>New in {2}</1> below.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>II.</1> Online Dispute Resolution (ODR) Platform & Digital Service": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "New": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>III.</1> Commencement of Proceedings & Pleadings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>IV.</1> Case Management & Hearings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>V.</1> Evidence & Discovery": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>VI.</1> The Arbitral Tribunal": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>VII.</1> Arbitral Proceedings & Awards": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>VIII.</1> Mediation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>IX.</1> Conciliation Procedure": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>X.</1> Specialized Corporate ADR": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>XI.</1> Implementation and Enforcement": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>XII.</1> Costs & Fees": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>XIII.</1> Miscellaneous": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute exists to provide parties with a fair, efficient, and dependable alternative to litigation. A procedure is only as trustworthy as the principles that govern it. This Code therefore begins with the Moral Principles that bind the Institute, its Secretariat, and every arbitrator, mediator, and conciliator acting under it.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "This edition brings dispute resolution online. The move to digital proceedings changes the room in which justice is done, not the standards by which it is done. The principles below apply equally to every proceeding, whether conducted in person or through the Adjudix E-Portal.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "These principles are binding, and every provision of this Code shall be read and applied in accordance with them.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The parties shall be treated with equality, and each shall be given a full opportunity to present its case, whether the proceeding is conducted in person or online.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Digital Trust": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Electronic records shall be kept secure, access to them limited to those entitled, and online proceedings conducted so that no party is disadvantaged by the medium.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "VIII": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "“Adjudix E-Portal”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "means the online platform of the Institute through which proceedings are filed, notices served, records maintained, and virtual hearings conducted.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "“hybrid hearing”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "means a hearing in which some participants attend in person and others by video conference.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "“virtual hearing”": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "means a hearing conducted by video conference through the Adjudix E-Portal or another platform approved by the Secretariat.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "It governs arbitration, mediation, conciliation, and corporate dispute resolution administered by the Institute, whether conducted in person, online, or partly in each.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter II</1>Online Dispute Resolution (ODR) Platform & Digital Service": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "New in {0}": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The Adjudix E-Portal and Digital Portal Standard": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Every proceeding under this Code may be filed, administered, and conducted through the Adjudix E-Portal, which shall maintain the official record of the proceeding.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The Secretariat shall publish the technical standards of the E-Portal, including supported file formats, size limits, and minimum requirements for virtual hearings, and shall ensure that the E-Portal is accessible to parties without specialist equipment.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Where a party is unable to use the E-Portal, the Secretariat shall provide reasonable assistance or permit filing by other means.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Before a proceeding is conducted online, the Secretariat shall explain to the parties, in plain language, how the online proceeding will be conducted, the role of the neutral, and the safeguards for their data, so that their participation is informed.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Filing of Electronic Pleadings and Statements": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Pleadings, statements, applications, and documents may be filed electronically through the E-Portal and shall be deemed filed on the date and at the time recorded by the E-Portal.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Documents shall be filed in a searchable format where practicable, paginated, and accompanied by an index.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "A document filed electronically shall be treated as an original unless the neutral directs production of the original for inspection.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Digital Service of Notices and Process": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Any notice or communication under this Code may be served by uploading it to the E-Portal, by email, or by any other electronic means through which the addressee has communicated in relation to the dispute or which the addressee has designated.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Service is deemed effected on the day the notice is transmitted, provided that the record of transmission does not show a failure of delivery.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Where electronic service cannot be effected, notice may be served by courier or registered post to the last known address of the addressee.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Electronic Signatures, Authentication, and Verification": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Any document required to be signed under this Code may be signed by an electronic signature recognised under the Information Technology Act, {0}.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The Secretariat may verify the identity of any participant before granting access to the E-Portal or to a virtual hearing.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Confidentiality, Data Security, and Storage of Digital Records": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The Secretariat shall maintain the E-Portal with reasonable security practices, and shall restrict access to the record of each proceeding to the parties, their representatives, the neutral, and authorised staff.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Electronic records shall be retained for such period after the conclusion of the proceeding as the Secretariat may determine, and shall thereafter be securely deleted, save as the law requires.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter III</1>Commencement of Proceedings & Pleadings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "In an arbitration, the statement of claim and the statement of defence, together with any counter-claim or set-off, shall be completed within six months of the date on which the arbitrator or all the arbitrators received written notice of their appointment, in accordance with Section {0}({1}) of the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter IV</1>Case Management & Hearings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "As soon as practicable after constitution, the neutral shall convene a case management conference with the parties, which may be held by video conference.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "At the conference, the neutral shall, after hearing the parties, settle the procedural timetable, the manner of taking evidence, whether hearings will be in person, virtual, or hybrid, and any other procedural matter. The timetable, and any modification of it, shall be communicated to the Secretariat and the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Conduct of Physical, Virtual, and Hybrid Hearings": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Hearings may be conducted in person, as virtual hearings, or as hybrid hearings, as the neutral directs after consulting the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "A virtual or hybrid hearing shall be conducted so that every participant can see and hear every other participant and the documents under consideration, and the neutral shall ensure that no party is prejudiced by the medium.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "If a technical failure prevents a party, a witness, or the neutral from participating fully in a virtual or hybrid hearing, the neutral shall suspend or adjourn the hearing, or take such other steps as are necessary, so that no party is prejudiced.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The neutral shall give the parties sufficient advance notice of every hearing. Unless the parties agree otherwise, hearings shall be held in private, and no person who is not involved in the proceeding shall be admitted without the approval of the neutral and the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "<1>Chapter V</1>Evidence & Discovery": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "The evidence of a witness shall ordinarily be given by written statement, and the witness shall attend the hearing, in person or by video conference, for cross-examination if the neutral so directs.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021",
 "Electronic records, including emails, messages, and data from electronic systems, may be relied upon as evidence. The neutral may require such certification as to the source and integrity of an electronic record as the neutral considers appropriate, guided by Section {0}B of the Indian Evidence Act, {1}.": "/dispute-resolution/rules/code-of-procedure/2021"
}
